1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Kaio's late. Again.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
But she said she was gonna give me my present today.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Maybe she was up all night making it and overslept.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Satoru?

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Yeah.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Satoru?

7
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Yes, sir!

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Everything all right?

9
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Or is there something on your mind?

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Kaio?

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Open up, it's me!

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Kaio!

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Oh no.

14
00:00:47,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Rubber boot tracks. Too big to be a kid's. It snowed two nights ago. And these tracks are fresh. Whoever was here was an adult. Probably male.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Shit. Now what do we do?

16
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:25,000
It's the girls festival and we'll have fun.

17
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,500
kissing chill few days.

18
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Number three.

19
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
About two.

20
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:59,180
立ち止まって 振り返って 止めどない今日を嘆き合った

21
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:05,360
記憶だって 永遠にだって 残らないもんと思い知って

22
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:10,920
僕がずっとかきむして 心隅っこで泣いた

23
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:16,000
そしてどうか 失くさないでよって後悔した

24
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:24,000
過ぎる日々を後悔してんだよって そう言い逃したあの日

25
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:30,000
君を待った 僕は待った 途切れない明日も過ぎてって

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:37,000
僕は今日もかきむして 忘れない傷をつけてるんだよ

27
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:43,000
忘れない downloading

28
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
忘れないどうなる

29
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
忘れない後悔した

30
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
忘れないでしょ

31
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
忘れないでしょ

32
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:57,000
あーオウ wins

33
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:03,000
忘れないでしょ

34
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:10,220
I didn't go back to school for two days.

35
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:15,800
Hmm. I guess Mom went to the store.

36
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:21,400
I found out a kid got snatched not too long ago, over in the next town.

37
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:23,880
But the cops already caught that scumbag.

38
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:28,120
This guy is someone new. We have to warn people before he does it again.

39
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:31,200
The problem is the police put a gag order on the story.

40
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:33,500
What about airing it when kids aren't watching?

41
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:35,320
The station could do that easy.

42
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:38,580
And I can go talk to the school and see if they'll issue a warning.

43
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:41,880
Okay. I'll talk to the boss about your idea.

44
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:43,340
I'd appreciate it.

45
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:47,540
He's a reporter for Ishikari TV. My mom used to work with him.

46
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:52,660
The last thing I want is for Satoru to grow up with horrible memories like this.

47
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:53,660
I hear you.

48
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:56,420
Making me forget was her idea.

49
00:03:56,420 --> 00:04:01,440
I know you're worried, but you've got to eat something.

50
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:03,420
What happened isn't your fault, kiddo.

51
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:07,160
I tried, but I couldn't help her.

52
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:08,820
I don't know about that.

53
00:04:09,860 --> 00:04:12,520
I just... I didn't want her to be alone.

54
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:14,840
And thanks to you, she wasn't.

55
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:17,740
It wasn't enough. I should have done more.

56
00:04:17,740 --> 00:04:21,040
Look, what happened, happened.

57
00:04:21,460 --> 00:04:23,600
So it's pointless to beat yourself up about it.

58
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:28,180
In a situation like hers, there's only so much anyone could have done.

59
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,220
That goes for you and me.

60
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:32,500
You should go back to school tomorrow.

61
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:35,320
You'll just feel worse staying here alone.

62
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:36,400
Okay.

63
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:37,140
Good.

64
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:38,500
Now eat up, okay?

65
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:39,980
Yeah.

66
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:45,380
I, uh, have a confession.

67
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:48,860
The other day I told you Kaio was home with a cold.

68
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:50,040
That's not true.

69
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:54,400
She's staying with her grandmother in Sapporo for personal reasons.

70
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:57,960
It happened so fast, she didn't have a chance to say goodbye.

71
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:00,180
But don't worry. I hear she's doing well.

72
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:04,200
She ran away.

73
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:06,840
I heard Kaio's mom hit her with a broom.

74
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,220
Oh my god, really?

75
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:10,400
Hey, it's better she's with her grandma.

76
00:05:10,940 --> 00:05:11,940
Hey, Satoru!

77
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:14,300
Cheer up, man!

78
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:16,480
Yeah, don't worry. You'll see her again.

79
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:17,200
Mm-hmm.

80
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:24,460
Satoru, the school and the PTA talked about it and decided this was for the best.

81
00:05:24,860 --> 00:05:27,980
I hate to ask this, but could you go along with the story?

82
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:29,060
Sure.

83
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:30,820
I'm sorry.

84
00:05:32,620 --> 00:05:34,700
The press couldn't talk about it either.

85
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:39,800
And for the past few days, the police had a car parked outside Kaio's house.

86
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:44,820
They were watching it because they pegged her mom as the prime suspect.

87
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:50,820
Then, six days after Kaio disappeared.

88
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:58,360
Listen up, everyone. I have an announcement.

89
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:01,820
From now on, when you leave school, make sure you're either with your parents...

90
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:05,960
The next girl was kidnapped sooner than she should have been.

91
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:10,800
You hear about Aya Nakanishi?

92
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:14,920
I don't know if you knew her, but she was a student at Izumi Elementary.

93
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:16,160
I heard.

94
00:06:16,740 --> 00:06:20,900
I have a friend who goes there, and he said she ran away to go live with her grandfather.

95
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:24,000
She did, huh? Just like Kaio.

96
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:27,720
She didn't run away. That's a lie.

97
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:33,160
If you ask me, there's a kidnapper on the loose.

98
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:42,780
The details might not be exactly the same, but things were definitely following the same flow of time as before.

99
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:50,600
Stations ran stories on the missing girls all day, except Ishikari TV.

100
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:53,840
They only ran them early in the morning and late at night.

101
00:06:54,340 --> 00:06:58,300
So, parents were advised to have their kids watch Ishikari TV only.

102
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:00,420
I'm home!

103
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:13,760
After Aya Nakanishi went missing, I noticed something.

104
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:17,320
The cops had dialed back their stakeout at Kaio's place.

105
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:21,100
They must have realized a serial kidnapper was on the loose.

106
00:07:30,420 --> 00:07:45,440
Ten days after Kaio disappeared, I saw her mom toss out a bag of trash.

107
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:48,700
A pair of mittens was in it.

108
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:53,120
I'll give you your present tomorrow.

109
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:54,700
Promise.

110
00:07:54,700 --> 00:08:19,840
Where am I?

111
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:32,540
I'm back in 2006 again.

112
00:08:35,420 --> 00:08:37,960
Address 23-1, 4th Street.

113
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:39,840
Victim, Sachiko Fujinuma.

114
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,160
Femus, 52.

115
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:44,760
Suspect is her son, Satoru Fujinuma, 29.

116
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:46,880
We're talking to the eyewitness now.

117
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:48,220
Over.

118
00:08:52,220 --> 00:08:53,800
Are you Satoru Fujinuma?

119
00:08:53,940 --> 00:08:54,080
No.

120
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:55,540
It wasn't me.

121
00:08:56,260 --> 00:08:57,140
I didn't do it.

122
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:00,180
God damn it.

123
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:02,040
I couldn't save Kaio.

124
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:03,820
Mom's still dead.

125
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:05,980
Everyone still thinks I killed her.

126
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:08,520
I couldn't change anything after all.

127
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:11,840
Only one thing to do.

128
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:13,360
Run.

129
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:22,800
I'm hiding under a bridge in a box.

130
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:24,680
Talk about cliches.

131
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:27,220
I wonder if I made the news yet.

132
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:27,240
I wonder if I made the news yet.

133
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:29,660
Come on, think.

134
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:31,880
Why was Mom murdered?

135
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:34,400
Did she know who the killer was?

136
00:09:35,060 --> 00:09:37,800
When I found her, I didn't see her phone anywhere.

137
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:39,040
Or her bag.

138
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:40,600
They were both gone.

139
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:42,680
The killer took them.

140
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:43,720
But why?

141
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:48,540
I bet she had evidence on him, and he was scared the cops would find it.

142
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:56,980
I'm crashing hard.

143
00:09:56,980 --> 00:10:00,260
If I only had a day to sleep, I'd think better.

144
00:10:00,260 --> 00:10:09,200
There you go.

145
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:10,000
Eat up.

146
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:10,720
Thanks.

147
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:13,020
I'm sorry about work today.

148
00:10:13,300 --> 00:10:14,400
It's no big deal.

149
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:16,300
One no-show won't get you fired.

150
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:18,240
Irie was worried about you, though.

151
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:21,500
Well, I wasn't, because I figured you had a pretty good reason.

152
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:24,060
We can talk about it after we eat.

153
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:25,160
Thanks.

154
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:29,600
That sucks.

155
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:31,760
The fight with your mom was that bad, huh?

156
00:10:32,540 --> 00:10:32,940
Yeah.

157
00:10:33,940 --> 00:10:35,360
That's the trouble with old folks.

158
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:36,360
They could be hella stubborn.

159
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:40,780
You can crash here as long as you want, but your mom's your mom, so try and patch things

160
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:41,200
up with her.

161
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:42,240
I will.

162
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,260
Hey, you want a beer?

163
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:45,100
No.

164
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:46,780
Crap, I'm all out.

165
00:10:46,780 --> 00:10:49,360
I'm going to go out and get some more.

166
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:56,600
He's kind of a knob, but his heart's in the right place.

167
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:58,540
I feel bad for lying.

168
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:03,540
Police rushed to the apartment after receiving an anonymous tip.

169
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:07,680
Inside, they found the body of a woman believed to be the tenant's mother.

170
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:12,920
The suspect, described as a male in his late 20s, fled the scene before he could be questioned.

171
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:15,300
The police are currently searching the neighborhood for him.

172
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:16,340
This is not good.

173
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:18,120
This is so not good.

174
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:20,740
And now the sports minute.

175
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:25,820
Japan's soccer team is heading for the playoffs in Germany today for what some are calling

176
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:26,460
the most anti-

177
00:11:26,460 --> 00:11:30,040
I should have known he'd screw me over.

178
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:31,640
What am I saying?

179
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:32,640
I can't blame him.

180
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:34,500
He was just trying to do the right thing.

181
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:36,800
If I was in his shoes, I'd do the same.

182
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:37,860
God damn it.

183
00:11:37,860 --> 00:11:50,720
You're an idiot.

184
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:55,200
Irie?

185
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,500
No way!

186
00:11:56,540 --> 00:11:58,320
You called me by my first name?

187
00:11:58,500 --> 00:11:59,280
That's a first.

188
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:02,580
You know, if you're on the run, you shouldn't leave your phone on.

189
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:05,040
The police can use GPS to track you.

190
00:12:05,580 --> 00:12:05,940
Oh.

191
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:09,240
Are you just gonna sit there?

192
00:12:09,540 --> 00:12:10,580
Hop on, let's go.

193
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:12,560
Come on, shake a leg.

194
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,720
Sorry about this, Katagiri.

195
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:24,260
Call me Irie.

196
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:26,680
It's one of the perks of writing Tandem.

197
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:29,180
I can't believe you let me in your house.

198
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,500
You do know why they're after me, right?

199
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:33,720
The cops came to see the manager today.

200
00:12:33,980 --> 00:12:35,620
I overheard them talking about it.

201
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:37,080
It was on the news, too.

202
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:39,680
Then why'd you risk helping me get away?

203
00:12:39,860 --> 00:12:41,400
Because you didn't kill her, that's why.

204
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:44,540
At dinner, I could see how much you guys meant to each other.

205
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:45,580
That's a fact.

206
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:49,520
Yeah, well, thank you.

207
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:51,220
You don't have to thank me.

208
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:54,700
I can't imagine what you're going through and to have the cops after you, too.

209
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:56,400
You don't deserve that.

210
00:12:57,560 --> 00:13:00,780
No one deserves the kind of stuff you've been through before, either.

211
00:13:01,260 --> 00:13:01,620
What?

212
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:04,660
This.

213
00:13:05,560 --> 00:13:07,200
You left it behind at work the other day.

214
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:10,700
One of the chapters had a sticky, so I went ahead and read it.

215
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:13,760
Talked all about what happened in your hometown when you were a kid.

216
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,900
How Kyo Hinazuki was murdered.

217
00:13:17,220 --> 00:13:18,760
I cried when I read it.

218
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:21,380
She died the day of the girls' festival.

219
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:23,340
Wait, it says that?

220
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:24,300
Yeah.

221
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:26,940
It says she died on March 3rd.

222
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:30,760
Anyway, make yourself at home.

223
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:33,620
I have to take the bike back before they miss it.

224
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:37,460
And don't even think about leaving this room.

225
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:44,940
This isn't how it was before.

226
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:47,300
It changed.

227
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:49,000
I changed it.

228
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:52,160
If I can go back again, I can save Kyo.

229
00:13:52,160 --> 00:14:03,340
Oh, yeah.

230
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:04,760
I'm in Irie's room.

231
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:06,780
Dear Satorial,

232
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:09,680
I think I should stick to my normal schedule today,

233
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:11,880
so I'm going to work my usual shift.

234
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,540
The fam said they'd be leaving the house around 10

235
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:17,080
and won't be coming back till after 8 tonight.

236
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:21,540
The key to the house and my bike are next to my clock.

237
00:14:22,620 --> 00:14:23,760
Here's the number to my cell.

238
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:26,640
Wait.

239
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:28,780
I thought her last name was Katagiri.

240
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:32,260
Thank you, Mr. Nishizono.

241
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:34,460
I can't tell you how much we appreciate it.

242
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:37,800
Well, your father's done so much for me.

243
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:39,440
I wish I could do more.

244
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:40,600
Oh, God, no.

245
00:14:40,920 --> 00:14:42,300
Believe me, you've done enough.

246
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:44,080
Heck, my dad couldn't be happier.

247
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:46,800
Thanks to that stoplight and crosswalk you approved,

248
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:49,100
we get more customers now than ever before.

249
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:49,840
Please.

250
00:14:50,100 --> 00:14:51,400
Your business is doing well

251
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:53,560
because your father is a shrewd businessman.

252
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:56,280
All I did was give him a little boost.

253
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:57,160
That's all.

254
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:59,400
Besides, it's a school route.

255
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:00,840
Safety first, you know?

256
00:15:01,020 --> 00:15:02,760
The city council's been talking about

257
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:04,500
putting a stoplight here for ages.

258
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:06,280
I left the receipts by the till.

259
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:07,280
Heading home.

260
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:08,100
Sure.

261
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:09,700
Nice hustle today, Irie.

262
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,320
What you got there?

263
00:15:11,740 --> 00:15:13,720
Oh, just some leftover pizza.

264
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:14,920
Leftovers?

265
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:15,620
Are you kidding?

266
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:17,160
Go on, get a fresh one.

267
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:17,660
My treat.

268
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:18,940
Thanks for the offer, boss.

269
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:20,060
But this'll do.

270
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:22,420
My friend won't know the difference anyway.

271
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:25,060
Oh, I hope she likes it then.

272
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:27,700
That is if your friend's a, you know, girl.

273
00:15:28,020 --> 00:15:30,340
Yeah, well, see you tomorrow.

274
00:15:33,420 --> 00:15:35,040
She's a cute girl, huh?

275
00:15:36,020 --> 00:15:37,400
Yeah, I guess.

276
00:15:37,580 --> 00:15:39,240
If you're into that sort of thing.

277
00:15:39,580 --> 00:15:40,440
I mean, she's 17.

278
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:41,980
She's just a kid.

279
00:15:41,980 --> 00:15:46,060
Yeah, well, I should get back to the office.

280
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:49,840
Thanks for stopping by, sir.

281
00:15:49,840 --> 00:16:03,940
Hey, Irie!

282
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:06,500
What's up?

283
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:06,960
Here.

284
00:16:07,340 --> 00:16:08,480
You forgot to take this.

285
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:10,620
It is part of the promotion, after all.

286
00:16:10,980 --> 00:16:12,360
Oh, okay, thanks.

287
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:13,800
I was wondering,

288
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:15,840
have you talked to Satoru lately?

289
00:16:16,340 --> 00:16:16,680
No.

290
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:19,840
I can't believe he'd just up and kill his own...

291
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:21,680
I mean, you know, what they're saying he did.

292
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:23,200
It's not like the guy at all.

293
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:24,560
No, it isn't.

294
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:26,480
I don't know how tight you guys were,

295
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:27,360
but if you see him,

296
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:29,400
do what you can to help him, okay?

297
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:30,280
Sure.

298
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:32,060
Let him know we're on his side.

299
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:33,880
And if you talk to him, give me a shout.

300
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:35,520
Yeah, I totally will.

301
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:43,400
What am I doing?

302
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:45,400
I doubt I'm going to find anything.

303
00:16:48,180 --> 00:16:51,080
A kid disappeared here three years ago.

304
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:53,860
Yeah, I think I remember this.

305
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:57,240
And three weeks later, they arrested some guy for it.

306
00:16:57,660 --> 00:17:00,300
Even after the trial, he swore he was innocent.

307
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:03,880
It's a hell of a coincidence.

308
00:17:05,140 --> 00:17:06,740
Or is it?

309
00:17:06,740 --> 00:17:22,920
Why would you want to go and call the police for?

310
00:17:24,020 --> 00:17:24,580
Iri...

311
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:27,480
Is that why you wanted me to help Satoru?

312
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:29,660
You said you were on his side.

313
00:17:29,740 --> 00:17:30,660
You said that!

314
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:32,580
Wait a sec, Iri.

315
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:33,780
I just...

316
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:36,100
I was worried about you, that's all.

317
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:44,120
If all you wanted was to get him caught,

318
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,360
you should have told me the truth!

319
00:17:45,580 --> 00:17:46,700
I trusted you!

320
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:48,700
I trusted you and you lied to me!

321
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:51,200
I didn't want to see you get hurt.

322
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:52,100
I swear.

323
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:54,860
That, I believe.

324
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:56,640
I'm sorry.

325
00:17:57,140 --> 00:17:58,880
Boss, please.

326
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:01,620
If you're really worried about me,

327
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:04,040
then don't call the police over here.

328
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:06,580
I don't want my family getting involved in this.

329
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:18,520
I'm sorry, Satoru.

330
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:20,260
Nah, it's no big deal.

331
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:22,000
I got to sleep a bit.

332
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:25,040
So thanks for letting me stay and conk out on your floor.

333
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:26,660
No, don't mention it.

334
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:28,380
I just wish you could go back.

335
00:18:28,380 --> 00:18:29,200
It's okay.

336
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:30,880
It's better if I don't.

337
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:34,280
By the way, that's not your parents' house, is it?

338
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:35,100
Uh-uh.

339
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:37,480
I'm staying with my uncle and his wife.

340
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:39,380
My town doesn't have a high school.

341
00:18:40,060 --> 00:18:40,960
It's out in the boonies,

342
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:42,480
so I had to come to the city for it.

343
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:43,940
I asked my uncle,

344
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:45,700
and he said I could stay with them in Chiba.

345
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:49,220
Mind if I ask a weird question?

346
00:18:49,860 --> 00:18:50,200
Uh-uh.

347
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:52,880
Like, why do you believe me?

348
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:55,040
You don't even know me all that well.

349
00:18:56,740 --> 00:18:57,860
You're right, I don't.

350
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:58,680
But I don't care.

351
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:00,380
I want to believe you.

352
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:03,800
When I was in elementary school,

353
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:06,540
my dad took me grocery shopping one day.

354
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:11,940
The owner stopped my dad

355
00:19:11,940 --> 00:19:13,980
and accused him of stealing a candy bar.

356
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:16,180
Like I said, my town's small,

357
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,380
so the owner knew my dad.

358
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:19,600
He said if he just admitted stealing it,

359
00:19:19,620 --> 00:19:20,540
he'd drop the whole thing.

360
00:19:21,140 --> 00:19:22,100
But he refused,

361
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:23,560
and the owner kept pushing him.

362
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:26,600
I never heard my dad yell before,

363
00:19:26,980 --> 00:19:28,600
but that day he went off.

364
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:31,600
The owner ended up calling the police,

365
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:34,720
and since my dad belonged to the local farmer's co-op,

366
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:37,460
they gave him a three-month suspension as punishment.

367
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:39,860
You didn't steal it, Daddy!

368
00:19:39,960 --> 00:19:40,360
I know!

369
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:42,640
I saw you didn't do anything wrong!

370
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:44,740
After what happened,

371
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:46,380
Dad quit the co-op,

372
00:19:46,740 --> 00:19:47,400
divorced Mom,

373
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:48,320
and left.

374
00:19:49,540 --> 00:19:51,800
I guess my mom thought he really stole it,

375
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:53,620
like everyone else in town.

376
00:19:53,620 --> 00:19:58,380
If someone believes in you,

377
00:19:58,780 --> 00:19:59,480
you're not alone.

378
00:20:00,100 --> 00:20:01,600
And if I was in your situation,

379
00:20:01,860 --> 00:20:03,280
I'd want someone to believe me.

380
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:06,420
I think you should go home.

381
00:20:06,780 --> 00:20:08,440
Tell the cops I forced you to hide me.

382
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:09,760
They'll buy that story.

383
00:20:10,180 --> 00:20:11,100
God, you're an idiot.

384
00:20:11,540 --> 00:20:13,320
You can't deal with this on your own,

385
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:14,900
and I won't lie to the police.

386
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:18,280
Okay, but could you not call me an idiot anymore?

387
00:20:19,220 --> 00:20:20,140
No promises.

388
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:22,860
I'll be back in a sec

389
00:20:22,860 --> 00:20:24,480
with a change of clothes and stuff for you.

390
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,160
The boss didn't call the police after all.

391
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:31,260
Good for him.

392
00:20:32,740 --> 00:20:32,880
Hmm?

393
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:41,860
But it can't be.

394
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:45,060
What is this?

395
00:20:45,700 --> 00:20:46,720
It can't be from him

396
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:48,740
because he told me his mom's phone was gone.

397
00:20:48,740 --> 00:20:50,520
Unless he found it.

398
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:51,280
No.

399
00:20:51,740 --> 00:20:52,760
It's from the killer.

400
00:20:53,780 --> 00:20:54,780
He's after me now.

401
00:20:59,220 --> 00:21:00,360
Oh my God.

402
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:04,240
Gotta get out.

403
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:06,360
I gotta...

404
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:07,360
I gotta...

405
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:22,380
I gotta...

406
00:21:22,380 --> 00:21:43,380
僕だけが見てた君のこと 過去も未来も 悲しみも喜びも すべて

407
00:21:43,380 --> 00:21:54,380
大人になるってきっと 優しくなることだと信じていた

408
00:21:54,380 --> 00:22:04,380
子供の頃も僕のままに 君のこと守りたいと思う

409
00:22:04,380 --> 00:22:10,380
暗闇から目覚めても 僕を待ち受けてる

410
00:22:10,380 --> 00:22:16,380
彼方で二人を隠した この街に

411
00:22:16,380 --> 00:22:22,380
誰も知らない 雪が降っていた

412
00:22:22,380 --> 00:22:31,380
君は僕の胸に 刻まれた一番深い 傷跡のようで

413
00:22:31,380 --> 00:22:45,380
君が笑う この世界の歌 乗り戻すよ

